  "notes": "Measured on the 787-9 (B-208S, right side) and checked on the A320neo and A330 from the left; the sweep's curves are approximate (oblique photos). 'Hainan Airlines' starts about x 0.31 on the 787; set nearer the Chinese here as on the A320neo. The door outlines in red-orange aren't drawn. Colors by eye. Re-checked 2026-11-15: kept as measured on the 787-9 (drawnOn B789). The commonest type is the 737-800, where the sweep is laid out differently: on B-7172 (2024-11-25, right side, fitted to the B738 shape) the red reaches the window line only at x ~0.6 and the crown just ahead of the fin, a second gold band runs from there up the fin's leading edge, and the titles sit at x 0.19-0.27 (Chinese) and 0.28-0.43; drawn on the 737 from these areas the red covers the aft windows from x ~0.45. A 737 version needs the sweep redrawn from 737 photos (not done in this re-check). Hainan Airlines' lowercase 0.66 of the capitals.",
  "history": "New entry (not in Skyarium v1): Hainan Airlines, HNA Group's flagship, flies its own red-and-gold Dapeng scheme under its own code."
